<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="46868" href="schedule/2019/spring/ARTS/299/46868.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="ARTS" href="schedule/2019/spring/ARTS.xml">Art--Studio</subject><course id="299" href="schedule/2019/spring/ARTS/299.xml">Spec Topics in Studio Art</course></parents><sectionNumber>ME1</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Chainmaking</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Chainmaking.  ARTS 230 (Jewelry/Metal I) prerequisite.  This course will focus on the making of chains for jewelry designs and other wearables. Students will learn to fuse metal to make complex loop in loop chains, forge wire to give character to line, and make chain mail to create metal fabric. Students will design jewelry and related objects while exploring metal as a medium of personal aesthetic expression.</sectionText><sectionFeeAmount>Art  Design Metals $95.00 Flat Fee.</sectionFeeAmount><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ST ">Studio</type><start>09:00 AM</start><end>11:40 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>221</roomNumber><buildingName>Architecture Annex</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Theide" firstName="B">Theide, B</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>